{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And in their statutes you shall not walk.</b> That a person should not accustom himself to walk in this way until it becomes for him a statute." "And <b>the deeds of the land of Egypt.</b> Concerning the laws and the sight — \"their laws you shall do\" is written about the laws in the Book of the Covenant, explained in the portion \"These are the laws.\""], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The phrase 'the sight' (והראיה) is textually difficult; read hyper-literally. 'Their laws you shall do' may resolve a citation abbreviation; the reference appears to be to Exodus 21–24, the section beginning 'And these are the judgments' (ואלה המשפטים)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:39.217447490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}